=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p> </p></li><li><p>Gap Fill: When price action gaps, and then immediately moves the opposite direction to fill the gap. </p></li></ul><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><a class=\"image-link image2 is-viewable-img\" target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFUt!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFUt!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFUt!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFUt!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFUt!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFUt!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png\" width=\"1347\" height=\"866\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/a510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:866,&quot;width&quot;:1347,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:203419,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/207431657?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFUt!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFUt!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFUt!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!iFUt!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fa510228e-65e0-4464-82d1-9096e0a8774b_1347x866.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div class=\"image-link-expand\"><div class=\"pencraft pc-display-flex pc-gap-8 pc-reset\"><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container restack-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 20 20\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" stroke=\"var(--color-fg-primary)\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" class=\"icon-noB79L\"><g><path d=\"M2.53001 7.81595C3.49179 4.73911 6.43281 2.5 9.91173 2.5C13.1684 2.5 15.9537 4.46214 17.0852 7.23684L17.6179 8.67647M17.6179 8.67647L18.5002 4.26471M17.6179 8.67647L13.6473 6.91176M17.4995 12.1841C16.5378 15.2609 13.5967 17.5 10.1178 17.5C6.86118 17.5 4.07589 15.5379 2.94432 12.7632L2.41165 11.3235M2.41165 11.3235L1.5293 15.7353M2.41165 11.3235L6.38224 13.0882\"></path></g></svg></button><button tabindex=\"0\" type=\"button\" class=\"pencraft pc-reset pencraft icon-container view-image buttonBase-GK1x3M\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-maximize2 lucide-maximize-2 icon-noB79L\"><polyline points=\"15 3 21 3 21 9\"></polyline><polyline points=\"9 21 3 21 3 15\"></polyline><line x1=\"21\" x2=\"14\" y1=\"3\" y2=\"10\"></line><line x1=\"3\" x2=\"10\" y1=\"21\" y2=\"14\"></line></svg></button></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>The larger the market cap, and more volume, the more likely a gap will fill. However the question is “when.” Yes the gap may fill, but if you get into a continuation run, then the trade can be extremely painful, last a long time. </p><p>Personally, I take gaps as a trend signal most often. Even if the price action pulls back, and fills the gap, that moment in time indicates a significant change in price action, and usually indicates a big volume move. <strong>I would much rather buy a stock gapping up, as it provides a much higher probability that the trade will be profitable, if not immediately, in the future. </strong></p><p class=\"button-wrapper\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Subscribe now&quot;,&quot;action&quot;:null,&quot;class&quot;:null}\" data-component-name=\"ButtonCreateButton\"><a class=\"button primary\" href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/subscribe?\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p><h4><strong>Position Sizing</strong></h4><p>My general rule, is that you should never take more than -3% risk to your total portfolio equity. Generally. One of the most common mistakes I see, is people with small accounts trying to double or triple their account in 1 trade. You may get a few wins with this, but this wild approach will eventually burn you. <strong>Don’t do it. </strong></p><p><strong>When taking risk with a position you have two options:</strong></p><ol><li><p>Tighter stop: less % risk. </p></li><li><p>Smaller position size: higher % risk, but less $ risk.</p></li></ol><p>Because I switched to longer term trading, so we could ignore headlines and the chaos in the world, my initial position sizes are smaller. <strong>I have beat this drum RELENTLESSLY.</strong> I add to the winning speculations, not the losers, compounding the wins and not the losses. </p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"><strong>Simple example with simple numbers:</strong></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">Total Portfolio Value: $100,000 </p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">-3% of total portfolio value is $3000</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">You want to buy a stock that is $100 per share</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">You want to take a -5% risk, which is $95 per share, or a $5 per share risk</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">Portfolio Risk / Position Risk = Shares you can buy</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">$3000 / $5 = 600 shares $60,000 of your portfolio</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">You can buy 600 shares at $100 with a -5% risk, and it will only impact your portfolio -3%.</p><p>But obviously, if you are longer term trading, A -5% stop on a mid-cap, volatile stock is not reasonable. Nor is putting $60,000 of your portfolio in, as post market activity can really put you in a bad situation (especially if it gaps!). </p><p>So lets REDUCE OUR POSITION SIZE</p><p>Lets say we decide to invest $5000 of our $100,000 portfolio into a stock. Again, max draw down for total portfolio we will take is -3% or -$3000. </p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">$5000 worth of shares = 50 shares</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">Dollar loss per share = $3000 (risk to portfolio) / 50 shares = $60 per share</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">$60 per share is what we would sell at, resulting in -$3000 to total portfolio, or -3%</p><p style=\"text-align: center;\">Stop will be -60% from $100, which is at $40 per share. </p><p>See how much more volatility you can endure, by decreasing position size? Again, this was a simple example. People pooping their pants over a stock, I can tell they are over positioned in a stock, or worse, using leverage. </p><p>I do have a high hit rate, not to sound egotistical…been doing this for a while. But <strong>the only guarantee I can give you, is that I WILL GET SOME WRONG. I PROMISE! The best traders on the earth get some wrong. </strong></p><p>If you need to trim some…trim. If my trading style goes against yours, don’t do it! If you need to cut a position…CUT! It is ok, it is just part of the game. Build your game plan BEFORE you enter a trade. </p><p>The Portfolio risk calculator is linked up above. </p><p>I hope this helps you, if you have any questions, feel free to ping me in the main chat. And be sure to take some breaks this weekend. Staring at red charts will not make them go up, nor will you solve the mysteries of the market. Staying fresh for the following week, will help you far more.</p><h4>Be sure to like and re-stack also! Its the only way we beat out the AI slop on social media. </h4><p>Thanks for stopping by! </p><div class=\"community-chat\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://open.substack.com/pub/tjstocks/chat?utm_source=chat_embed&quot;,&quot;subdomain&quot;:&quot;tjstocks&quot;,&quot;pub&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:3537822,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Timothy’s StockTok&quot;,&quot;author_name&quot;:&quot;StockTok 📈&quot;,&quot;author_photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!r3SF!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F545d5c5a-3f40-44b0-b1a1-980901ed236d_565x565.png&quot;}}\" data-component-name=\"CommunityChatRenderPlaceholder\"></div><p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p><p style=\"text-align: center;\"></p>",
